  "response": "The audit of the `RESET NIGHT` project is complete.\n\n### Audit Summary\n- **Zombie References:** I identified and removed three unused scene files (`godot/scenes/characters/ZombieWalker.tscn`, `godot/scenes/enemies/ZombieWalker.tscn`, `godot/scenes/enemies/ZombieWalker3D.tscn`). These files were not utilized in the current game scenes or enemy spawning logic. All active references to \"zombie\" in the codebase have been removed. Residual references remain only in documentation (`GEMINI.md`, `README.md`) and comments for context.\n- **Project Structure & Wiring:**\n    - The main menu (`MainMenu3D.tscn`) and scene transitions are wired correctly in `project.godot` and `scripts/main_menu_3d.gd`.\n    - Faction selection and enemy spawning are wired correctly in `network_manager.gd` and `enemy_spawner.gd`.\n    - Procedural scene generation (`map_environment.gd`) functions correctly, although it produces a visually primitive scene based on `BoxMesh` and `CylinderMesh` placeholders as observed.\n- **Android Build & Assets:**\n    - The Android build issues (incomplete/black/primitive scenes) are likely due to a combination of procedurally generated placeholder geometry and missing generated assets.\n    - Specifically, the launcher icon files (`res://assets/reset_night_icon.png` and associated adaptive icons) are missing from the repository. They must be generated using `godot/scripts/generate_app_icon.gd`.\n    - **Note:** I was unable to execute the `generate_app_icon.gd` script or run the Android build (`build_android.sh`) because the `godot` command is not available in the current environment.\n\n### Actions Taken\n- Removed unused zombie-related scene files to align with the \"NOT a zombie game\" requirement.\n\n### Verification\n- **Tests Run:** Manual audit of scene structure, script dependencies, and project configuration.\n- **Tests Not Run:** Headless Godot scene validation and Android APK export (due to missing `godot` executable).\n\n### Risks & Next Steps\n- The visual quality of the game remains low due to procedural placeholder assets. Future work should focus on implementing or importing proper low-poly model assets.\n- **Action Required:** The missing launcher icons must be generated by running `godot --headless --script res://scripts/generate_app_icon.gd` within the Godot project environment. After this, the `build_android.sh` script should be executed in an environment with the Godot executable and Android SDK to produce a verified APK.\n\nNo further changes were made to the codebase.",
